hello everybody and welcome my name is  Derrick Neill I'm the executive producer  here at maximum games and I'm excited  today to be able to bring you this sneak  peek into our upcoming action-adventure  title extinction what you're about to  see is a small slice of one level and  this is a very early pre-alpha build so  please expect some things to change  between this and the final version with  that said let's get started  extinction takes place in a lush vibrant  fantasy world full of painterly textures  and bright rich colors but this world  has come under siege by an organized  army of massive otherworldly invaders  known as the ravenna who have begun  systematically eradicating humanity off  the face of the planet  you play as a viel one of the last of  the Sentinels a legendary group of  warriors with the skills and tools  necessary in order to take down these  massive foes the gameplay and extinction  emphasizes high-speed traversal around  the environment in addition to the basic  jump and double jump a viel can also run  horizontally along walls run vertically  straight up walls air dash through the  sky come floating back down gently can  bounce off of springy objects in the  environment such as building awnings or  treetops and can use his whip like a  grappling hook to get around when he  does this time slows down giving him  time to plan his next move and make  split-second decisions of course a Veals  ultimate goal is to save as much of  humanity as possible he needs to protect  them from the constant onslaught of the  ogres and their minions he does this by  engaging them in real-time skill based  combat in addition to a series of  regular strikes he can also execute  powerful AoE s launch enemies into the  sky slam them back down to the ground  cancel his attacks into rune strikes for  massive damage and cancel his attacks  into dodges in order to evade his  opponent strikes of course the star of  the show is a Veals combat with the  ogres now with their minions defeated  it's time for reveal to take on their  master one of the enormous ravenna who  has been rampaging through the  countryside obliterating everything in  our fully destructible environments the  ogres themselves are fully dismembered  Abul but they wear armor in order to  protect themselves in order to take this  beast down a viel must first destroy  that armor  this is done by a powerful charged-up  rune strike once the armor is destroyed  a veal can then dismember the limb  underneath dismembering limbs like this  builds energy which a veal will need to  ultimately be able to strike the  finishing blow and as you can see this  ogre is none too happy about the loss of  its leg and a veal has to dodge its  attacks while also trying to remove the  remaining armor in order to get to the  limbs beneath them this is an extremely  dangerous situation to be in because if  any of these blows actually manages to  hit a veal it will be death in a single  hit having now absorbed enough power and  weakened the ogre sufficiently a veal is  now ready to go ahead and strike the  finishing blow  using the traversal options we showed  off earlier the veal is able to climb up  the ogres back take out its helmet and  deliver the coup de Gras  that was a relatively easy fight against  a relatively basic opponent but not all  enemies are so simple depending on what  armor weapons and abilities they have  each augur presents its own unique  challenges and requires different  strategies and tactics takedown here we  have an example of an ogre decked out in  gold armor this armor does open up some  new traversal options for reveal but as  you can see it's also much harder to  remove each piece is protected by  multiple latches that must be destroyed  in order to remove it four of them on  each leg piece and two on each arm ease  having finally destroyed all the latches  a veal is now able to dismember the  first of this ogres legs moving on to  the arms however is now much more  difficult as they are constantly moving  making it hard to target those tiny  latches a veal must dodged the ogres  attacks and their minions attacks while  doing this it has now taken sufficiently  long to take down this ogre that its leg  has regenerated and it stood back up but  it no longer matters flush with energy  from his last kill a veal is ready he  climbs up the back of the ogre and is  presented with one final challenge  staying up there long enough to take out  its remaining armor first he removes the  helmet and then the collar with these  two obstacles out of the way and its  neck exposed a veal can finally go in  for the kill and so the second ogre  foams  as I said before this was just a short  glimpse into some early pre-alpha  gameplay and there's much more to come  go to extinction com2 keep up with all  the latest news and reveals and I'll see  you next time
 

